# The build context is the repository root: the image COPYs bin/otterd and
# bin/otter from it, so the context cannot be narrowed to this directory.
# Everything else is excluded, because a context carrying .git, the test suite
# and local caches makes the build slower and gives the image more inputs than
# it has.
*
!packaging/container/**
# Include the whole bin directory rather than naming the two files. Naming them
# individually is ambiguous under prefix matching -- "bin/otter" is a prefix of
# "bin/otterd" -- and an exclusion that drops the daemon fails the build with
# "checksum ... /bin/otter: not found" for a file that plainly exists. The
# Dockerfile COPYs exactly the two binaries it needs, so including the directory
# grants nothing extra.
!bin
